## Files changed

**`src/range.ts`** — Rewrote `overlaps`:
- Added a `parse` helper that calls `Date.parse` and throws `TypeError` with `"Invalid date: ${value}"` if `NaN`.
- After parsing all 4 endpoints, checks `a.end < a.start` and `b.end < b.start`, throwing `RangeError` with the offending values.
- Returns `false` early if either range is zero-length (start === end), since an empty range contains no moments.
- Otherwise returns `aStart < bEnd && bStart < aEnd` (strict `<`, end-exclusive).

**`src/range.test.ts`** — Added 11 tests (keeping the original 1):
- 2 touching-range tests (a before b, b before a) → `false`
- 1 same-start non-empty → `true`
- 1 empty vs itself → `false`
- 1 empty vs normal (both orders) → `false`
- 1 two empty at same instant → `false`
- 2 unparsable start (first arg, second arg) → `TypeError` with bad value in message
- 1 unparsable end → `TypeError` with bad value in message
- 2 end-before-start (first arg, second arg) → `RangeError`

